    passageB2: `<p>The world was <strong>horrified</strong> by the terrible acts of terrorism in the United States. These actions have been rightly condemned by leaders worldwide, who see such terrorist activities as a <strong>serious threat</strong> to democracy and a <strong>grave crime</strong> against the American people.</p>
<p>Terrorist acts are often <strong>deliberately designed</strong> to gain maximum publicity for the cause the terrorists support. The terrorists who crashed planes into the World Trade Center in New York certainly achieved <strong>widespread attention</strong>. The second plane attack was even broadcast live on television news channels around the globe, capturing the moment of impact.</p>
<p>The desire to <strong>publicise their aims</strong> usually leads terrorist groups to claim responsibility for acts of violence. However, immediately after the attack on America, no group <strong>stepped forward</strong> to take responsibility. Also, terrorist attacks on civilian targets often include some kind of warning. This <strong>was not the case</strong> in New York, and thousands of innocent people lost their lives.</p>
<p>The United States invests heavily in defence and intelligence. Yet, the country was completely <strong>taken by surprise</strong> by this attack. Many Americans had believed their powerful nation was <strong>invulnerable</strong> and were deeply shocked that terrorists could <strong>breach their security</strong> in such a way.</p>
<p>There are many different terrorist groups around the world, each <strong>driven by</strong> different motivations. These might include a feeling of political injustice, religious <strong>zeal</strong>, or simply hatred for those they attack. They are often a <strong>hidden enemy</strong>, using <strong>secrecy</strong> to commit brutal acts, and then disappearing without a trace. </p>
<p>The most difficult terrorists to deal with are those who are prepared to die for their cause. Their <strong>fanatical hatred</strong> of their targets means they are willing to commit suicide to inflict casualties on the enemy. World leaders now understand the global nature of many modern issues. The need to <strong>eliminate terrorism</strong> is, without doubt, one of the most important.</p>`,
    translationB2: `<p>Dunyo Qo'shma Shtatlarda sodir etilgan dahshatli terrorchilik harakatlaridan <strong>dahshatga tushdi</strong>. Bu harakatlar butun dunyo bo'ylab yetakchilar tomonidan haqli ravishda qoralandi, ular bunday terrorchilik faoliyatini demokratiyaga <strong>jiddiy tahdid</strong> va Amerika xalqiga qarshi <strong>og'ir jinoyat</strong> sifatida baholaydilar.</p>
<p>Terrorchilik harakatlari ko'pincha terrorchilar qo'llab-quvvatlaydigan maqsad uchun maksimal darajada ommaviylikni ta'minlashga <strong>qaratilgan</strong>. Nyu-Yorkdagi Jahon Savdo Markaziga samolyotlarni urib tushirgan terrorchilar, albatta, <strong>keng e'tiborga sazovor bo'lishdi</strong>. Hatto ikkinchi samolyot hujumi butun dunyo bo'ylab televizion yangiliklar kanallarida jonli efirda namoyish etilib, zarba momenti aks ettirildi.</p>
<p>O'z <strong>maqsadlarini e'lon qilish</strong> istagi odatda terrorchilik guruhlarini zo'ravonlik harakatlari uchun javobgarlikni o'z zimmasiga olishga undaydi. Biroq, Amerikaga qilingan hujumdan so'ng darhol hech qanday guruh javobgarlikni o'z zimmasiga olish uchun <strong>oldinga chiqmadi</strong>. Shuningdek, tinch aholi nishonlariga qilingan terrorchilik hujumlari ko'pincha qandaydir ogohlantirishni o'z ichiga oladi. Nyu-Yorkda esa <strong>bunday bo'lmadi</strong> va minglab begunoh odamlar hayotdan ko'z yumdilar.</p>
<p>Qo'shma Shtatlar mudofaa va razvedkaga katta sarmoya kiritadi. Shunga qaramay, mamlakat bu hujumdan butunlay <strong>hayratda qoldi</strong>. Ko'pgina amerikaliklar o'zlarining qudratli davlatlari <strong>daxlsiz</strong> deb hisoblagan edilar va terrorchilar bunday yo'l bilan o'z <strong>xavfsizliklarini buzishi</strong> mumkinligidan chuqur hayratda qolishdi.</p>
<p>Dunyo bo'ylab turli xil terrorchilik guruhlari mavjud, ularning har biri turli xil motivlar bilan <strong>boshqariladi</strong>. Bularga siyosiy adolatsizlik hissi, diniy <strong>g'ayrat</strong> yoki shunchaki o'zlarining nishonlariga nisbatan nafrat kirishi mumkin. Ular ko'pincha <strong>yashirin dushman</strong> bo'lib, shafqatsiz harakatlarni sodir etish uchun <strong>maxfiylikdan</strong> foydalanadilar va keyin izsiz g'oyib bo'ladilar.</p>
<p>Eng qiyin terrorchilar - bu o'z maqsadlari uchun o'lishga tayyor bo'lganlardir. Ularning nishonlariga nisbatan <strong>fanatik nafrati</strong> dushmanga talafot yetkazish uchun o'z joniga qasd qilishga tayyor ekanliklarini anglatadi. Dunyo yetakchilari hozirgi zamonaviy masalalarning global xarakterini tushunishadi. <strong>Terrorizmni yo'q qilish</strong> zarurati, shubhasiz, eng muhimlaridan biridir.</p>`,
